@flexiarg ways-of-working/selection-gives-a-reason
@title A selection gives a reason over ways of selecting, and a click can be refused
@keywords way of working, invariant, cascade live
@audience agents, operators, institution designers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-11-02 by claude-16; runs correct it
@provenance declared in futon3c/holes/excursions/ways-of-working.json (claude-2 with Joe, 2026-11-02)
@why [creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions creativity-commons/affected-participants-change-the-rules]

! conclusion: No outer-then-inner click runs unless the selection report names the way of selecting that won and what it would have proposed otherwise.

  + IF:
    Deciding what to do next, accountably, under uncertainty, with the goals themselves formable.

  + HOWEVER:
    A selector can return a choice that looks computed: a score, a tie broken at random, or a pick from items it never read.

  + THEN:
    No outer-then-inner click runs unless the selection report names the way of selecting that won and what it would have proposed otherwise.

  + BECAUSE:
    A choice that cannot state what it compared cannot be corrected, and goals have to be formable, not assumed.

  + VALIDATION:
    Does the selection report name the way of selecting that won, and what the alternatives would have proposed?
